	doi = {10.1021/acsami.3c07537},
	abstract = {MnTe is considered a promising candidate for nextgeneration phase change materials owing to the reversible and nonvolatile phase transformation between its α and β’ phases by irradiation of a nanosecond laser or application of a pulse voltage. In this work, for a faster phase control of MnTe, the response of metastable βMnTe thin films to femtosecond (fs) laser irradiation was investigated. Using ultrafast optical spectroscopy, we inferred transient phase transformation. Moreover, with an increase in laser-excitation fluence, a nonvolatile structural change from the β to α phase was experimentally observed by Raman spectroscopy and transmission electron microscopy without ablation damage on the sample. The observation results strongly suggest that the fs-laser-induced β → α phase transformation proceeds through the nucleation and growth mode without a large temperature increase.},
