	doi = {10.1039/C8EE00923F},
	abstract = {Artificially synthesized n-type Sb
              2
              Se
              3
              with a low work function produces abrupt photocurrent generation
              via
              a novel surface charge-inversion mechanism.
            
          , 
            
              Binary chalcogenide Sb
              2
              Se
              3
              shows dominantly p-type electrical conductivity and poor photocathodic performance; however, its narrow band gap and low work function suggest satisfactory conditions for the generation of the inversion state at the surface if used as a photoanode. We propose a fabrication design for the synthesis of n-type Sb
              2
