	doi = {10.1109/PVSC43889.2021.9518895},
	abstract = {In this work, we study antimony selenide (Sb2Se3) thin film solar cells deposited by closed space sublimation followed by a post-deposition selenization process at different temperatures. Scanning electron microscopy and X-ray diffraction analyses are employed to investigate the effects of the selenization treatment on the structural properties of Sb2Se3 films. It is found that a proper selenization temperature leads to a highquality Sb2Se3 film with the desired grain orientation and a benign Sb2Se3/Mo interface. After optimizing, we obtained Sb2Se3 solar cells with an improved power conversion efficiency from 3.66 to 7.07 \%.},
